Proposed test for `tests/test_rbtree_whitebox.c` — the "two children, root, real fixup" case from the plan. Hand-built tree: `d`(B) root with `b`(B) left, `f`(B) right; deleting `d` promotes successor `f` into the root slot and should trigger a real case-2 rebalance (sibling `b` recolored red). I'll assert on the tree's exact resulting shape/colors (not `rb_find`, since these hand-built nodes carry `NULL` values) to prove the fixup logic actually ran rather than passing vacuously:

```c
static void test_delete_two_children_root_triggers_fixup(void) {
    rb_node_t *b = make_node("b", RB_BLACK);
    rb_node_t *f = make_node("f", RB_BLACK);
    rb_node_t *d = make_node("d", RB_BLACK);
    d->left = b;
    b->parent = d;
    d->right = f;
    f->parent = d;
    rbtree_t *t = make_tree(d, 3);
    assert(rb_validate(t) == 0);

    /* Successor of "d" is "f" (z's direct right child, itself black), so
     * y_original_color is BLACK and delete_fixup actually runs: case 2
     * fires on x_parent=f/w=b (both of b's children are NIL/black), which
     * should recolor b red and leave f as the new black root. */
    assert(rb_delete(t, "d") == 0);
    assert(rb_size(t) == 2);
    assert(rb_validate(t) == 0);
    assert(strcmp(t->root->key, "f") == 0);
    assert(t->root->color == RB_BLACK);
    assert(t->root->left != NULL && strcmp(t->root->left->key, "b") == 0);
    assert(t->root->left->color == RB_RED);
    assert(t->root->right == NULL);
    rb_destroy(t);
}
```

Also want to fix the header comment at lines 5–10 in the same file, which still says "`rb_delete` isn't implemented yet" — that's stale now:

```c
